      "title": "Ministers to end Palantir’s contract with NHS in England in 2029",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/16/ministers-to-end-palantir-contract-nhs-england-2029",
      "description": "<p>DHSC to extend US tech firm’s contract for two more years to allow time to line up British companies to replace it</p><p>Ministers will end the NHS’s contract with the controversial tech firm Palantir – but not until 2029, to allow time to line up British companies to replace it.</p><p>The Department of Health and Social Care (DHSC) has decided to extend Palantir’s contract to provide the federated data platform (FDP) – the software that links different healthcare providers – for two more years rather than exercise a break clause that would have let them axe it next spring.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/society/2026/nov/16/ministers-to-end-palantir-contract-nhs-england-2029\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-16T19:59:31"
    },
    {
      "title": "UK companies line up to replace Palantir in NHS",
      "link": "https://www.ft.com/content/f69f1f6b-cdbe-40d6-b76d-fb712ca58b51?syn-25a6b1a6=1",
